# Entrypoints and test fixtures are consumed by bash and by Python on Linux
# runners. CRLF in a shebang line makes the interpreter unfindable, so keep
# these LF regardless of the platform they are checked out on.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
run text eol=lf

# The corpus is data, not source, and some of it asserts things about the bytes
# themselves. One scanner test is about CRLF line endings, and normalising it on
# the way into the repository would delete the only thing it tests while leaving
# a green check behind. Nothing under here gets converted, in either direction.
reference/tests/** -text

